tification fails the gate, and a\nsanction whose pattern has disappeared fails it too."},"2758":{"id":"/project-conventions-851","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"A `glob()` whose pattern has no wildcard is a plain file name wearing a\ndisguise: write the string."},"2759":{"id":"/project-conventions-852","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"Anything a target reads at runtime belongs in its `data` list. When you add a\nmanifest that `scripts/lib/*.sh` applies, add its filegroup to `//scripts:manage`."},"2760":{"id":"/project-conventions-853","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#writing-it-bazel-first","content":"New package: give it a `\"\"\"Package purpose: …\"\"\"` docstring and a public `:all`\naggregate, then list that aggregate in `//:everything`."},"2761":{"id":"/project-conventions-854","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-check","content":"Follow the `doc_coverage` shape: `tests/<name>.py` with `_repo_root()` and\n`_tracked()`, a `main()` that prints `  - <path>: <reason>` to stderr and returns\n1, a three-line `tests/<name>.sh` wrapper, a `tests/test_<name>.py` unit suite run\nby `tests/<name>_unit.sh`, two `sh_test` targets in `tests/BUILD.bazel`, and the\nlabels added to `_TEST_FAST` in the root `BUILD.bazel`. Then add a row to the\ncoverage-gate table above and to tests/README.md."},"2762":{"id":"/project-conventions-855","page_id":"/project-conventions","tags":["conventions","contributing","safety","bazel","style"],"type":"text","url":"/project-conventions#adding-a-new-inferenc