itch port map, movable orchestrator — and the Ansible artifacts generated from it."],[766,"The declarative topology `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml` is the single source of truth for\n**all five configurations** — node names/IPs, fabric, switch port map, and which Spark is\nthe orchestrator. Edit it, then render:"],[623,"The deployment mounts an `emptyDir` at `/data` with:"],[243,"The devcontainer image already includes these CLIs; on the host, install them or use the devcontainer."],[202,"The docs targets install missing npm dependencies on first run, so a fresh clone needs no separate setup step."],[2745,"The doctor is the bootstrap that proves `bazelisk` is installed, so it cannot depend on `bazelisk`. Everywhere else uses `bazelisk run //:doctor`."],[711,"The driver container may take several minutes to load after first boot."],[1613,"The estimator will warn you if free GPUs look insufficient."],[1833,"The exact NVFP4 397B checkpoint (\\~250 GB) requires **4 nodes**. On smaller clusters, use `qwen-agentic-spark-1` (122B NVFP4) or `qwen-agentic-spark-2` (397B int4-AutoRound) — see `qwen_tiers` in `config/nemotron-catalog.yaml`."],[3689,"The file is `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml`. The engine is `scripts/lib/py/lab_topology.py`\n(shell wrapper: `scripts/lib/topology.sh`). `bazelisk run //:manage -- setup` and\n`bazelisk run //:manage -- topology` drive it."],[3543,"The five supported configurations"],[146,"The following are modeled with first-class Bazel targets:"],[1326,"The full stack (`mcp-agent-toolkit-full`) uses `nemotron-retriever-embed` for document chunk embeddings and Qdrant for retrieval — the same RAG pillar as Nemotron and Qwen agentic presets."],[51,"The generated trees are ordinary content to the site: `//docs-site:*` targets depend on\n`//docs:content`, which globs `docs/generated/**` alongside the hand-written pages, so a\nregenerated reference invalidates the build and the sidebar picks the new headings up with no\nextra wiring."],[235,"The generator lives in `docs/generate_shell_docs.py`. It is intentionally kept simple (stdlib only) but is being improved for even nicer output formatting."],[42,"The generator now produces:"],[2633,"the generators whose output the site ships"],[2922,"The golden rule and why heavy workloads are dangerous around power events"],[1078,"The host `hermes-lab` stack is a **persistent lab operator*&#x2A;. Coder and Kasm workspaces use a separate &#x2A;*`workspace-dev`** profile for coding assistance:"],[608,"The image starts Hermes `workspace-dev` in the background on session launch. Desktop shortcuts open the dashboard (`:9119`) and Hermes CLI."],[1871,"The lab portal **Agent Chat** panel shows prerequisites, deploy/stop controls, and launch links."],[3033,"The lab uses **production-grade Traefik v3** (official Helm chart) as the unified HTTPS entry point, with **Authelia** for user management and forward-auth SSO. K3s bundled Traefik stays disabled; the standalone Helm install supports CRD middleware chains, TLS, and metrics."],[69,"The MkDocs site published two aliases with **mike**; Fumadocs has no mike equivalent, so the\nsame URLs are produced by building the static export twice with different `basePath` values:"],[3673,"The model"],[3636,"The model is TP=1 (many Nemotron nano/super, Qwen3.6 dual, MedGemma)"],[1031,"The multi-arch **devcontainer** can install the Hermes **CLI** (`hermes`) for\nlocal agent-assisted coding — see dev-environment.md.\nThat is separate from this page’s **host Docker gateway** on DGX Spark nodes.\nNever commit API keys or `hermes/data/.env` from either path."],[2155,"The multi-arch `.devcontainer/` image (linux/amd64 + arm64) includes bazelisk, buildifier, shfmt, ruff, mypy, ansible, kubectl, helm, kubeconform, shellcheck, bats, yamllint, Node.js 22, Python 3.11, Playwright, and a pinned Grok Build CLI. Versions and checksums are pinned in `.devcontainer/tool-versions.env` (shared with CI). Independent fetch stages keep rebuilds local to the pin that changed. Works on Apple Silicon, Windows (Docker Desktop + WSL2), Linux, and DGX Spark. See dev-environment.md."],[1723,"The Next.js control plane includes an **Observability** section (`#observability`):"],[709,"The NVIDIA GPU Operator works well on K3s but:"],[2980,"The old 64Gi policy floor reserved \\~192 GiB across three Sparks before any Job, so Mode A (\\~189 GiB) always failed and operators clicked through. That made the guard a paper tiger."],[2727,"The only cluster-operations entry point"],[3619,"The orchestrator name (not \"spark0\") is what the generated inventory and `group_vars`\nuse for `k3s_control_plane`. Inventory: generated from `ansible/inventory/lab.yaml`\n(legacy hand-made example: `ansible/inventory/hosts.ini.example`)."],[49,"The output is at `docs/generated/shell/reference.md` and appears in the site under **Reference > Code-Generated Reference**."],[782,"The playbook installs prereqs, highspeed netplan on 2+ nodes (from the generated per-node\nnetplan when present), K3s server on the **orchestrator** node (`role: orchestrator` in\n`lab.yaml`), agents, labels, kubeconfig."],[95,"The previous short paragraph has been replaced by this more complete description."],[1277,"The proxy must stay up if backends are down (per-model 503 is fine)."],[225,"The Shell Commands & Helpers page is **not** written by hand. It is produced from structured comments inside the scripts."],[3472,"The switch block (host, read-only user, `port_map`) lives in `lab.yaml`; the password is\n`LAB_SWITCH_PASSWORD` in the operator's environment only. Qwen 3.5 397B NVFP4 is the\ncanonical TP=4 Job here. Cabling and port map: Choose topology."],[3466,"The switch fabric is a managed 4× 400G QSFP-DD device; each node sees **one** RoCE link:"],[3583,"The switch is a managed 4-port 400G QSFP-DD device with a 10GbE management port:"],[3587,"The switch's management IP (e.g. `10.0.0.2`) is declared in the `switch:` block; only a\n**read-only** API probe may use it. The switch password is